%% Generated by render-integration.py; edit that script and run make diagrams.
sequenceDiagram
    box Proximtype
        participant PX as Application
        participant PDB as PostgreSQL
    end
    box Trade Maneuver
        participant MQ as RabbitMQ
        participant TM as TM application
        participant TDB as TM PostgreSQL
    end
    participant BR as Broker
    Note over PX,BR: RabbitMQ transport. At-least-once delivery. Deduplication by id.
    %% 01 / Producer publication
    PX->>PDB: Data + outbox (atomic)
    PX->>PX: Translate to the v1 contract
    PX->>MQ: publish tm.trade-signal.v1
    MQ-->>PX: publisher confirm → outbox: sent
    %% 02 / Signal intake and validation
    MQ->>TM: Deliver signal
    TM->>TDB: Check id in inbox
    Note over TM,TDB: Duplicate: ack and stop processing
    TM->>TM: Freshness, limits, session, kill switch
    %% 03 / Alternative paths: decline or approve
    alt decline
    TM->>TDB: inbox + SignalDeclined
    TM->>MQ: SignalDeclined
    else approve
    opt Manual mode
    Note over TM,BR: Manual mode / human approval required
    end
    TM->>TDB: inbox + Order (Approved)
    TM->>BR: Submit order with clientOrderId
    opt Timeout
    Note over TM,BR: On timeout: query order status with the broker.<br/>Do not submit the order again.
    end
    BR-->>TM: Confirmation / execution
    TM->>TDB: Persist Order state
    TM->>MQ: OrderFilled
    end
    %% 04 / Acknowledgement and result delivery
    TM-->>MQ: ack after commit
    MQ-->>PX: tm.trade-results → producer queue
    Note over PX,BR: Decline and approval are alternative paths. Results retain the signal identifier.
